ess model is  sort of underpinned and by our ability  to build you know relatively quickly use  an electrical network and then have  a number of retailers selling on our  behalf and what are some of the benefits  they're all getting any other retailers  the businesses and and the individual  end-users well I suppose if you look at  our our sort of our customers first  which are really the retailers and we  also obviously end customers but what  the retailers get is access to a  best-in-class system so we don't have  any of the issues that the legacy copper  systems would have so our IT platform is  brand new it's you know fit for purpose  today it hasn't been sort of cobbled  together over over many years from  upgrading this and upgrading that so if  you you know want to we call it Cyril  part if you want to come on to our  network as a retailer you use soil  report it's absolutely designed to be  user-friendly whereas I'd say some of  the incumbents across York's and  interfaces were not necessarily so  user-friendly so the retailer gets a  fantastic experience interfacing with us  and then the network is new it's on a  very robust and I like it built on a  very robust electrical network so the  reliability is very high in terms of the  service service levels that we can give  on it and obviously for the end consumer  then we're building a gigabit network so  they can get a gigabit of connectivity  into their home or into their business I  mean and that's that's the possibility  no I mean what excites me is I really  don't understand what you can do with a  gigabit but that's really the exciting  part is because there's lots of clever  people out there and kids coming through  and businesses and startup and  entrepreneurs that can take that  capacity and that yeah I think and build  fantastic businesses out of it and  obviously then you know at a residential  level you know it's entertainment drives  it but it's really then he help  eLearning working from home all the  stuff that internet connectivity so with  what the fiber-to-the-home council hears  about you know that sort of vision of  the future where fibre is ubiquitous and  everybody's able to benefit from their  you know the opportunity that it brings  more congratulations and what you've  done so far I'm sure we'll hear more  from you in the future thank you very  much Brian appreciate it so a unique all  fiber network spreading right across  Ireland  [Music]  you

